 ],
 "script": "Ice on the gutter? Easy. Homie's got a hammer!\n\nBonk! Bonk! Bonk!\n\nCrack! There goes the gutter. Whoops.\n\nHere's the thing. Ice dams form when the upper roof is above freezing, but the edge stays below thirty-two degrees.\n\nMelted snow refreezes at the edge, and the water backs up under your shingles.\n\nSo here's the real fix.\n\nOne. Stay on the ground, and gently pull snow off the roof edge with a roof rake.\n\nTwo. Clear your gutters and downspouts before the freeze.\n\nThree. Water stains on the ceiling? Call a roofer, and get the attic insulation and air leaks checked.\n\nIf Homie can handle it, so can you.",
 "audio_note": "Revid voice render was about 40.2 s of voice; audio.m4a is trimmed at 40.8 s and sped up 1.2x with ffmpeg atempo (pitch kept), caption times divided by 1.2",
